Hi Alex,

Here are the operations points from the call.

Volumes
- Normal day: about 18,000 order lines. Black Friday week: about 45,000 order lines
  a day, with the busiest hour around 4,000 lines.
- Our marketplace channel goes live in April 2027. We have no history for it and no
  forecast, and we won't have one before contract signature. It could add 10% or it
  could double our volume. Please size with headroom for it and price that headroom
  as an allowance, rather than waiting for a number from us that won't come.

Product data
- Dimensions and weights in Dynamics 365 are unreliable. A spot check of 300 SKUs
  last year found a lot of errors, but we never measured the rest.
- We don't know how many of the 22,000 SKUs are wrong. We'll only find out when every
  SKU goes over the measuring machine during the data load, and some will need
  re-measuring, photos or a new storage profile. Please allow for that clean-up
  effort; we can't tell you its size in advance.

Decisions that are ours, still open
- Carton range: our packaging team decides the carton sizes for the carton erector
  and the auto-bagger. They haven't settled on how many sizes or which ones yet; we'll
  send you the list once they have.
- Returns: we haven't decided whether returns processing is in this phase or the
  next. The board decides that with the budget.
- Acceptance testing: we haven't agreed internally who prepares the test orders and
  expected results for acceptance testing, or how many super-users we can release
  for testing. We'll come back to you.

Thanks,
Hannah Reid
Head of Operations, Harbourline Home & Garden
